<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Bfcm marketing stays off; transactional only</td><td>Bfcm consent is the legal basis of every send</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Bfcm education and proof before any offer</td><td>First-touch bfcm codes create discount dependence</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Bfcm cart reminder first; earn the discount decision</td><td>Guards bfcm margin while intent peaks</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Suppress bfcm selling after checkout; educate instead</td><td>Bfcm suppression protects the new-customer glow</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Hold bfcm marketing while service cases stay open</td><td>Bfcm messaging lands badly during open cases</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Remove chronic bfcm non-openers pre-complaint</td><td>Shields bfcm sender reputation and inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Hold bfcm texts to quiet hours and frequency limits</td><td>Bfcm SMS risk exceeds email per complaint</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Bfcm wholesale accounts get dedicated messaging</td><td>Bfcm contract buyers need separate rules</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Screen bfcm free/disposable emails before flows</td><td>Low-grade bfcm signups drag deliverability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Strip bfcm test data from live journeys</td><td>Bfcm reporting stays clean without test noise</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Treat bfcm snoops under normal consent policy</td><td>Ad-hoc bfcm exceptions break traceability</td></tr>
